{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>עומדות</b> — the meaning is: we stood to gaze at the structure of the walls and the beauty of the gates. And the correct interpretation: for it was full of people, and we would mingle at the gates, unable to enter because of the multitude of people coming and going."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 122, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:09.375007233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}